# Drone-Mapper-ex3 Context

TAU AdvCpp Assignment 3. Ex2's monolithic simulator is split into **three separately built projects**:
a `simulator_<ids>` executable that `dlopen`s an `Algorithm_<ids>.so` and a `MissionControl_<ids>.so`, and
runs many missions in parallel in either **comparative** or **competitive** mode.

Deadline: **Sep 6, 2026, 23:30**. Skeleton copied from `../ex_3_skeleton`; ex2 implementation in
`../Drone-Mapper-ex2` is the reference to port from.

## Authority order

1. `context/Advanced Topics TAU 2026B - Assignment 3.docx` (condensed in `docs/assignment3-checklist.md`)
2. Skeleton headers in `common/`, `Simulator/common_simulator/`, `MissionControl/common_mission_control/`
3. `context/Common issues and handling.pdf` and `context/Structuring the project.pdf`
4. `context/AdvCpp Review Guideline.docx` + `docs/review-error-codes.md`
5. Ex2 implementation — **ideas and logic only**, never a spec

When the skeleton README and the assignment doc conflict, the assignment doc wins. Unresolved conflicts
are tracked in `docs/open-questions.md` with a working assumption — follow the assumption.

## Layout

```text
common/                                    course-published, READ-ONLY, do not add files
Simulator/common_simulator/include/...     published simulator-only interfaces
Simulator/{include,src}/                   our simulator      -> simulator_<ids> executable
MissionControl/common_mission_control/...  published IDroneControl
MissionControl/{include,src}/              our mission control -> MissionControl_<ids>.so
Algorithm/{include,src}/                   our algorithm       -> Algorithm_<ids>.so
UserCommon/                                our shared code, NO build file (must be created)
inputs/                                    instructor maps and YAML configs
context/                                   assignment docx/pdf sources
docs/                                      condensed references
```

Placement decisions for every ported ex2 file: `docs/component-placement.md`.

